The sprite sheet (dist/fly-sheet.png, dist/fly-sheet.webp, and the copy embedded in
dist/fly.inline.min.js) is rendered from the NeuroMechFly body model through FlyGym 2.1.0,
replaying the recorded walking data that ships with FlyGym (flygym_demo.spotlight_data).
FlyGym and NeuroMechFly are developed at the Neuroengineering Laboratory (Ramdya lab), EPFL,
and are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: https://github.com/NeLy-EPFL/flygym

  - V. Lobato-Rios et al. NeuroMechFly, a neuromechanical model of adult Drosophila
    melanogaster. Nature Methods 19, 620-627 (2022). doi:10.1038/s41592-022-01466-7
  - S. Wang-Chen et al. NeuroMechFly v2: simulating embodied sensorimotor control in adult
    Drosophila. Nature Methods 21, 2353-2362 (2024). doi:10.1038/s41592-024-02497-y
